- ### Failure
+ ### Fallos

- A command which cannot be run at all, because its binary is missing, or is a directory, or is
- not executable, raises an `Exec.Error`. The error carries the command which failed, so it
- names what was attempted, instead of reporting an error number from the operating system:
+ Una orden que no se puede ejecutar en absoluto, porque falta su binario, o es un directorio, o
+ no es ejecutable, lanza un `Exec.Error`. El error lleva la orden que falló, así que nombra lo que
+ se intentó, en lugar de informar de un número de error del sistema operativo:

= names what was attempted, instead of reporting an error number from the operating system:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= names what was attempted, instead of reporting an error number from the operating system:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= names what was attempted, instead of reporting an error number from the operating system:
